FINAL CONCLUSION:

Cross-validation is a useful technique for evaluating machine learning models on multiple train-test splits. K-fold cross-validation provides a more reliable estimate of model performance, while StratifiedKFold ensures that class proportions remain similar across folds. A lower standard deviation indicates that the model's performance is more stable across different folds.
